content:
Her heart made of cotton and steel;
Softest touch can make her feel,
Fiercest blade won’t make a scar.

She has fallen, in the eyes of the mortal world;
But under her feet I see thousands of men
Who just fear and envy her.

Not even the thorns can hurt her;
Fleeting happiness can’t fade her desire.
Her prints were washed by the rain;
Her pains are just hormonal.

Her mind remains all fuzzed up;
Should pass the chain or, the might sword
To the daughter she carries in her womb.

The shackle she was born with, clasp her feet;
Did not let her run away so far.
Her body remains on the field;
The battle was too cruel for her.
